  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cross-Border Post-arrival Humanitarian Assistance to Undocumented Afghan Migrants from the Islamic Republic of Iran and the Islamic Republic of Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to a reduction in the vulnerability of returning Afghan migrants affected by economic downturn and humanitarian crises, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) will provide humanitarian assistance at IOM-run reception and transit centers in border provinces with the Islamic Republic of Iran and Pakistan to a total of 7,500 undocumented returnees. In addition, IOM is also continuing flow monitoring at four key border crossing points with Pakistan and Iran.</narrative>
  </description>
